    "description": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "New York City sits where the Hudson River meets the Atlantic, spread across five boroughs on islands and the mainland. Manhattan is about 21 km long and runs on a street grid laid out in 1811.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "The Dutch built New Amsterdam on the tip of Manhattan, and the English renamed it New York in 1664. More than 12 million immigrants passed through Ellis Island between 1892 and 1954. Bagels, pastrami on rye and the dollar slice came with them.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "text": "Late April to June and September to early November bring mild weather. Book Statue of Liberty crown tickets well ahead, as they sell out months in advance.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
